---
layout: null
permalink: /assets/glossary-index.json
---
{%- comment -%}
Machine-readable map of glossary term -> anchor id, generated from the glossary
page itself so the two can never drift apart. Consumed by academy.js, which
turns the first bolded occurrence of a known term in a lesson into a link to
its definition.

The glossary authors every entry as:  <dt id="term-x"><dfn>Name</dfn></dt>
so splitting on those two markers is enough to recover both halves. An entry
may also carry <span class="glossary-alias">other name / another</span>; each
alias is emitted as its own row pointing at the same anchor, so a lesson that
bolds "device driver" or "cvar" still links. The linker allows one link per
anchor, so a page that bolds two names for one entry gets a single link.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign glossary = site.pages | where: "permalink", "/glossary/" | first -%}
{%- assign chunks = glossary.content | split: '<dt id="' -%}
[
{%- assign first = true -%}
{%- for chunk in chunks offset:1 -%}
  {%- assign anchor = chunk | split: '"' | first -%}
  {%- assign halves = chunk | split: '<dfn>' -%}
  {%- if halves.size > 1 -%}
    {%- assign name = halves[1] | split: '</dfn>' | first | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- if name != "" -%}
      {%- unless first %},{% endunless -%}
      {%- assign first = false -%}
{"t":{{ name | jsonify }},"a":{{ anchor | jsonify }}}
      {%- assign alias_halves = chunk | split: 'class="glossary-alias">' -%}
      {%- if alias_halves.size > 1 -%}
        {%- assign alias_list = alias_halves[1] | split: '</span>' | first | strip_html | split: '/' -%}
        {%- for alias in alias_list -%}
          {%- assign alias_name = alias | strip -%}
          {%- if alias_name != "" -%},{"t":{{ alias_name | jsonify }},"a":{{ anchor | jsonify }}}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
